{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"I found the seed CSV contains 45 raw replicate observations with `StrainNumber` values for pure strains and `287_98` mixtures. The original analysis path filters out strain controls `1` and `98` (keeping `287` and `287_98`), derives frequency as the first ratio part over the sum, then fits quadratic, cubic, and `ns(..., df=4)` models in R. No ordinary Galaxy tool supports arbitrary R polynomial/spline fitting and optimization, so I’m using a pinned `r-base` BioContainer UDT that runs the R model fitting and reports the best model’s predicted maximum."}}
